KZ2 patch 6040: exclusive fullscreen on the live-draw swap chain survives a failed Present; ported
from Killzone 3 PC port patch 2130 (2026-10-29; same author, MIT; their patch is not in the
snapshot, so this follows their note, not their code). ENHANCEMENT / bug fix for patch 2095's code. Not yet confirmed
on native Windows (KZ3 waits for an outside tester too); only tried under Proton, which never reproduced the failure.
Two defects in 2095's present path, both not KZ-specific:
- No ResizeTarget/ResizeBuffers after SetFullscreenState: a flip-model swap chain needs a resize after every fullscreen
  transition, even when the client size did not change (2095 resized only on a size change, and borderless already had
  the output's size). Now rsx_live_draw_set_fullscreen asks for a forced resize after every successful transition, and a
  DXGI-made exit (Alt+Tab, mode change) is detected at the next present; the present then waits for the GPU, releases the
  back-buffer references, ResizeTarget (in exclusive fullscreen) and ResizeBuffers, before the Present.
- Any failed Present set g.ready = 0 for the session (the null backend, picture frozen, game running). Now
  ld_dm_present_failed: a device that is gone (GetDeviceRemovedReason) stops the renderer as before; any other failure
  leaves exclusive fullscreen (rsx_display_exclusive_lost posts it to the window thread: borderless for the session, the
  saved mode untouched), forces the resize and keeps drawing; 8 failures in a row stop it (rsx_present_recover.h). Every
  step is logged ([display]).
- KZ2_TEST_PRESENT_FAIL=N[@F]: N forced failures from live-draw frame F (default 300), for tests. Host test
  tools/runtime/test_present_recover.c.
- Also: the ResizeBuffers-failure path no longer reads a NULL back buffer.

